Document structure to write

Single markdown plan file at repo root (same location the user referenced). Suggested sections:

1. Overview and architecture

flowchart LR
  subgraph admin [Flutter Admin]
    Auth[Admin login]
    InvCRUD[Inventory CRUD]
    ProdKit[Product kits]
  end
  subgraph api [API /api/v1]
    InvAPI["/inventory"]
    ProdAPI["/products"]
    CatAPI["/inventory/categories"]
  end
  subgraph data [MongoDB]
    InvItem[InventoryItem stock source]
    Product[Product kit lines]
  end
  Auth --> InvAPI
  InvCRUD --> InvAPI
  ProdKit --> ProdAPI
  InvAPI --> InvItem
  ProdAPI --> Product
  Product -->|"items[].inventoryItem"| InvItem

Key concepts (plain language for Flutter devs):







Concept



Meaning



Example





stockQuantity



Count of warehouse units (packs)



50 packs





itemQuantity



Amount per stock unit



50





unit



Measure for itemQuantity



grams





totalAvailableQuantity



Virtual: stockQuantity × itemQuantity



2500 g





price / salePrice / currency



Per stock unit list/sale price (ZAR default)



R29.99/pack





effectivePrice



Virtual: sale if set, else price



R24.99





Product items[]



{ inventoryItem, quantity } — stock units per kit



2 packs per kit





Product stockQuantity (API)



Computed max kits buildable — not stored



read-only on product

Orders deduct InventoryItem.stockQuantity, not product-level stock ([inventoryService.js](src/services/inventoryService.js)).

2. Authentication







Step



Endpoint



Notes





Firebase sign-in



Client-side (password provider only)



Required before admin login





Admin login



POST /api/v1/auth/admin-login



Header: Authorization: Bearer <Firebase ID token>





Legacy alias



POST /api/v1/auth/admin/login



Same handler





API calls



All inventory routes



Header: Authorization: Bearer <accessToken> from login response data.accessToken





Refresh



POST /api/v1/auth/refresh



Body: { refreshToken }

Login success shape ([sendSuccess](src/utils/response.js)):

{
  "success": true,
  "data": { "accessToken": "...", "refreshToken": "...", "user": { ... } },
  "message": "..."
}

Flutter: store accessToken securely; attach to every /inventory and /products admin call.

3. Inventory category master data

21 codes in [src/masterdata/inventory/categories/constants.js](src/masterdata/inventory/categories/constants.js) (e.g. SACRED_POWDERS, FLOWERS_AND_LEAVES, … MISCELLANEOUS).







Method



Path



Role



Purpose





GET



/api/v1/inventory/categories



admin



Dropdown labels; query activeOnly=false to include inactive





POST



/api/v1/inventory/categories/seed



superadmin



refresh DB; use once per env if empty

Bootstrap flow: admin login → GET /inventory/categories → if empty, superadmin runs seed (or npm run seed:inventory-categories against Mongo).

4. Inventory CRUD API reference

Base: /api/v1/inventory. All require admin JWT.







Method



Path



Content-Type



Body / query





GET



/



—



Query: page, limit (max 100), search, category, status, lowStock=true





GET



/:id



—



—





POST



/



multipart/form-data



See create fields below + optional image file





PATCH



/:id



multipart/form-data



Partial update; optional image





POST



/:id/adjust-stock



application/json



{ "delta": 10, "reason": "delivery" } — delta non-zero integer





DELETE



/:id



—



Query ?hard=true for permanent delete

Create required fields ([inventoryValidation.js](src/validations/inventoryValidation.js)):





name, category (valid code), unit, itemQuantity (positive)



price (≥ 0), currency (e.g. ZAR)



Optional: salePrice, slug, description, stockQuantity (default 0), supplierName, lowStockThreshold, status (ACTIVE/INACTIVE)

Validation rules to surface in UI:





salePrice ≤ price (Joi + mongoose pre-validate)



Numeric fields may be sent as strings in multipart (backend coerces)



category stored uppercase

Example multipart create (curl-style for plan):

POST /api/v1/inventory
name=Turmeric powder 50g
category=SACRED_POWDERS
unit=grams
itemQuantity=50
stockQuantity=100
price=29.99
salePrice=24.99
currency=ZAR
lowStockThreshold=10
image=<file>

List response (data):

{
  "items": [ { "_id", "name", "slug", "category", "unit", "itemQuantity", "stockQuantity", "totalAvailableQuantity", "price", "salePrice", "currency", "effectivePrice", "isLowStock", "lowStockThreshold", "status", "imageUrl", ... } ],
  "pagination": { "page", "limit", "total", "totalPages" }
}

Adjust-stock response: data.item (updated row) + data.reason.

5. Product kit flow (admin)

Products remain separate merchandising layer with their own price / salePrice / currency (kit selling price), while inventory holds component unit pricing.







Method



Path



Notes





POST



/api/v1/products/create-product



multipart; items as JSON string





PATCH



/api/v1/products/:id



multipart partial update





GET



/api/v1/products/:id



stockQuantity enriched from inventory

items JSON (required on create):

[
  { "inventoryItem": "507f1f77bcf86cd799439011", "quantity": 2 }
]

quantity = stock units consumed per kit (not grams). Flutter: multi-select inventory rows → build this array → jsonEncode into form field items.

Other product fields: title, price, currency, optional salePrice, description, deity, category, status (DRAFT|PENDING), productStatus, image.

